  "security_implications": "sp_enc_err_d aggregates sparse-encoding errors (from sp2v_sig_err) into a single combinational flag; if not properly latched/sampled, a transient fault could go unnoticed. The data_in_prev_we and data_out_we signals are derived from specific bits of sp2v_sig_chk—if these bits are meant to carry integrity-protected write enables, a parameter misconfiguration (leading to out-of-bound index) could silently route unprotected or wrong signals, potentially bypassing sparse-encoding integrity checks on control paths.",
